-- title:
--   One layer of the layered node rings at a node of X(q²M')
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a prime $q$ and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$ the field $\bar F=$ `fieldBar q M'` is the intermediate field `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\subseteq$ `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** A valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is given with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$. Writing $A_0:=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$, the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it is a Henselian local ring and that its residue field is algebraically closed; `hκ` says that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Layer family of fields.** A type $\iota$ indexes intermediate fields $K(n)$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), together with valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K(n)$ characterised by $x\in A_n\iff x\in A$ (`hAn`), and a base index $n_0$ with $K(n_0)\le K(n)$ for all $n$.
--
--   The statement then fixes the algebra structure on $\bar F$ over $k_0$ obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\bar F$, and quantifies over the following data.
--
--   **The level field $F_0$.** An intermediate field $F_0$ of $\bar F/k_0$ such that the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$, and such that for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every family $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$ (linear disjointness of the constants from $F_0$).
--
--   **The valuation subring $W_0$ and the node ring $O$.** A valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with: for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ a discrete valuation ring; the maximal ideal of $W_0$ generated by the image of $\pi_0$. A subring $O$ of $F_0$, local and Noetherian, with: $O\subseteq W_0$; for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff the image of $x$ lies in $O$; every $f\in O$ differs from the image of some $x\in k_0\cap A$ by a non-unit of $O$ (constants surject onto the residue field of $O$); and every $f\in F_0$ satisfies $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in O$ with $h\neq 0$ (so $F_0$ is the fraction field of $O$).
--
--   **Crossing presentation of $\widehat O$.** A natural number $E_0\ge 1$, the fact that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, and a ring isomorphism $\iota_O$ from `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal ↥O) ↥O` onto the model $M_0:=$ `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat{A_0}\,(\hat\pi_0^{E_0})$, where $\widehat{A_0}$ is the completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, $\hat\pi_0$ the image of $\pi_0$ there, and `UVCrossingModel W π` is the quotient of the two-variable power series ring `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π`, with distinguished elements `U`, `V` and constants `const π w` the classes of the constant series $w$. Units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of $M_0$ are given, subject to: $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota_O$ carries the image of a constant $x\in k_0\cap A$ lying in $O$ to `const` of its image in $\widehat{A_0}$; $\iota_O(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota_O(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$; $c_y\in W_0$ and $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, while $c_x$ lies outside the maximal ideal of $W_0$ whenever it lies in $W_0$.
--
--   **Hasse germ.** The Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the series `jqModC` reparametrised by `qExpand` with parameter $q$) lies in $\bar F$; an element $a_0\in k_0$ is given such that $j-a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$; and for some $e_J\ge 1$ and some unit $w_V$ of $M_0$ one has $\iota_O(j-a_0)=w_V\cdot V^{e_J}$.
--
--   **Finite-type presentation of $O$.** A subring $B_x\subseteq O$ of $F_0$ such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at those $h\in B_x$ which become units of $O$ (precisely: $f\in O$ iff $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$), and such that $B_x$ is the subring generated by the images of the constants $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set $T$.
--
--   **The two ends.** A field $F_I$ over the residue field of $A$, a `RegularProlongation` $R_x$ of $A$ to $\bar F$ with residue field target $F_I$ (a valuation subring `integers` of $\bar F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism to $F_I$ whose kernel is its maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants), and a `Place` $b_x$ of $F_I$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring containing the constants, with principal ideals), such that: $b_x$ is rational (the constants surject onto its residue field); $O$ lands in $R_x$`.integers`; the $R_x$-residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of $b_x$, those of non-units of $O$ in its maximal ideal; the $R_x$-residue of $c_x$ is $0$; and $b_x$`.ord` of the $R_x$-residue of $c_y$ equals $1$. Symmetrically, a field $F_{SS}$ over the residue field of $A$, a regular prolongation $R$ with target $F_{SS}$ and a place $n_d$ of $F_{SS}$, with: for $f\in F_0$, $f\in R$`.integers` iff $f\in W_0$; $n_d$ rational; the $R$-residues of elements of $O$ in the valuation subring of $n_d$ and those of non-units in its maximal ideal; the $R$-residue of $c_y$ is $0$; and $n_d$`.ord` of the $R$-residue of $c_x$ equals $1$.
--
--   **Places and the ambient ring $\mathcal N$.** A set $S$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ characterised by: $P\in S$ iff $O$ is contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and, for every non-unit $f$ of $O$, the value $P$`.evalAt` $f$ lies in $A$ and in its maximal ideal; all members of $S$ are rational. A subring $\mathcal N$ of $\bar F$ characterised by $f\in\mathcal N$ iff $f$ lies in $R_x$`.integers`, in $R$`.integers` and in the valuation subring of every $P\in S$; and $P$`.evalAt` $f\in A$ for all $f\in\mathcal N$, $P\in S$.
--
--   **Layer coefficients.** Subrings $C'(l)\subseteq A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, each a discrete valuation domain, with elements $\varpi'(l)\in C'(l)$; discrete valuation domains $W_c(l)$, complete for the adic topology of their maximal ideals, with elements $\pi(l)$; natural numbers $e_L(l)$; and ring homomorphisms $j_c(l):C'(l)\to W_c(l)$, subject to: $c\in C'(l)$ iff $c\in A$ and $c$ lies in $K(l)$; $\varpi'(l)$ generates the kernel of the $A$-residue on $C'(l)$ in the sense that the $A$-residue of $d\in C'(l)$ vanishes iff $d\in\varpi'(l)C'(l)$; $C'(n_0)\le C'(l)$; $\pi(l)$ irreducible; $\pi_0=v\,\varpi'(l)^{e_L(l)}$ for some $v$ with $v,v^{-1}\in C'(l)$; $j_c(l)(\varpi'(l))=\pi(l)$; $j_c(l)(c)\in(\pi(l)^n)$ implies $c\in(\varpi'(l)^n)$; and every $w\in W_c(l)$ is congruent to some $j_c(l)(c)$ modulo $\pi(l)^n$, for every $n$.
--
--   **The layer to be constructed.** A layer index $l$ is fixed. Furthermore $\mathcal N_0$ is a subring of $\bar F$, local and Noetherian, characterised as $O$ read inside $\bar F$ ($f\in\mathcal N_0$ iff $f\in F_0$ and $f\in O$), and $N_1$ is a local Noetherian subring of $\bar F$ with $\mathcal N_0\le N_1$ subject to the hypotheses: $N_1\le\mathcal N$; $S$ is characterised by $N_1$, namely $P\in S$ iff $N_1$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and for every non-unit $f$ of $N_1$ the value $P$`.evalAt` $f$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; $C'(n_0)$ maps into $N_1$; every $g\in N_1$ differs from the image of some $o\in C'(n_0)$ by a non-unit; families $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $C'(n_0)$ admit no non-trivial relation $\sum_i c_i\cdot a_i=0$ with $a_i\in N_1$; the inclusion $\mathcal N_0\le N_1$ is local; the maximal ideal of $N_1$ is contained in the sum of the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal N_0$ and the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi'(n_0)$; for $f\in N_1$ inside $R_x$`.integers` one has $b_x$`.ord` of its residue $\ge 0$, with strict inequality when $f$ is a non-unit of non-zero residue, and likewise for $R$ and $n_d$; and $2\le$ `ringKrullDim` $N_1$. Finally, a last hypothesis requires a subring $B_x\subseteq N_1$ of $\bar F$ containing the images of $c_x$, $c_y$ and $u$, such that $N_1$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at those $h\in B_x$ which become units of $N_1$, and such that $B_x$ is generated by the image of $C'(n_0)$ together with a finite set $T$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of this there exists a subring $N_l$ of $\bar F$, local and Noetherian, such that: $N_1\le N_l$; if $l=n_0$ then $N_l=N_1$; non-units of $N_1$ remain non-units in $N_l$; $N_l\le\mathcal N$; $S$ is characterised by $N_l$, i.e. $P\in S$ iff $N_l$ is contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and for every non-unit $f$ of $N_l$ the value $P$`.evalAt` $f$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; $C'(l)$ maps into $N_l$; every $g\in N_l$ differs from the image of some $o\in C'(l)$ by a non-unit; no non-trivial relation $\sum_i c_i\cdot a_i=0$ holds with $a_i\in N_l$ and $c$ linearly independent over $C'(l)$; there is a subring $B_x\subseteq N_l$ containing the images of $c_x,c_y,u$, with $N_l$ the localisation of $B_x$ at those $h\in B_x$ which become units of $N_l$ and with $B_x$ generated by the image of $C'(l)$ together with a finite set $T$; the images of $c_x$ and $c_y$ lie in $N_l$, and the image of $u$ lies in $N_l$ and is a unit there.
--
--   Moreover there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma:W_c(l)\to$ `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal ↥Nl) ↥Nl` and a ring isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion onto `UVCrossingModel` $(W_c(l))\,(\pi(l)^{e_L(l)E_0})$ such that: $\sigma(\pi(l))$ is the image of $\varpi'(l)$ in the completion (whenever that image lies in $N_l$); $\iota_c(\sigma(o))=$ `const` $(\pi(l)^{e_L(l)E_0})\,o$ for all $o\in W_c(l)$; the element $j-a_0$ lies in $N_l$ and, for some $e\ge 1$ and some unit $w$ of the model, $\iota_c(j-a_0)=w\cdot V^{e}$; every $c\in C'(l)$ whose image lies in $N_l$ has that image of the form $\sigma(o)$ for some $o\in W_c(l)$; for every $f\in N_l$ lying in $R_x$`.integers` with non-zero $R_x$-residue and with $b_x$`.ord` of that residue equal to $n$, there is a unit $\gamma$ of the model with $\iota_c(f)-\gamma\cdot V^{n}$ in the ideal generated by `const` $(\pi(l)^{e_L(l)E_0})\,\pi(l)$ and $U$; and symmetrically, for every $f\in N_l$ lying in $R$`.integers` with non-zero $R$-residue and with $n_d$`.ord` of that residue equal to $n$, there is a unit $\gamma$ with $\iota_c(f)-\gamma\cdot U^{n}$ in the ideal generated by `const` $(\pi(l)^{e_L(l)E_0})\,\pi(l)$ and $V$.
--
--   This is the single-layer step in the construction of the layered rational node rings attached to a node of the semistable model of the full-level modular curve of level $q^2M'$: starting from the base node ring $N_1$ over the coefficient ring $C'(n_0)$, it produces the node ring $N_l$ over $C'(l)$ together with a crossing presentation $W_c(l)[[U,V]]$-style of its completion of thickness $e_L(l)E_0$, the Hasse germ of $j-a_0$ along one branch, and the two residue laws at the ends $(R_x,b_x)$ and $(R,n_d)$. It is stated for every prime $q$, so that it also serves the primes $q=2,3$, and it is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers_of_prime), which iterates it over the layer index set.
